    <values><field>Active__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:boolean">true</value></values><values><field>Advice__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Write down the steps: switch the agent off (and who may do so), preserve the logs, assess what was exposed, involve the DPO or privacy lead, and decide within 72 hours whether to notify the regulator.</value></values><values><field>Category__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">STAFF</value></values><values><field>Check_Type__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Manual</value></values><values><field>Critical__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:boolean">false</value></values><values><field>Handler__c</field><value xsi:nil="true"/></values><values><field>Level__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Implementation</value></values><values><field>Pass_Criteria__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">A documented incident process for this agent exists, with named people and a way to switch the agent off.</value></values><values><field>Question__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Is there a defined process for when the agent exposes data it shouldn't, covering who switches it off, who investigates, and who decides on a breach notification?</value></values><values><field>Resources__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">GDPR Article 33 - Breach notification|https://gdpr-info.eu/art-33-gdpr/</value></values><values><field>Sort_Order__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:double">780</value></values><values><field>Topic__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">T5</value></values>
